node_modules/
dist/

# Throwaway live-site probes (`probe.mjs`, `probe2.mjs`, ... at the repo root).
# One of these is a scratch script that drives Chromium against goofish to answer a
# single question, and it is not an artefact of the package -- the answer it produced is
# written down in CHANGELOG.md, where a later change can read it, and the script itself
# stays in git history for anyone who wants to re-run the measurement. Committing them
# put eleven of them on main, where a root full of `probe*.mjs` reads like tooling and
# invites the next one to be edited and re-landed.
/probe*.mjs

